    "notes": "Tuned continuation of the timed-release cooperative roles experiment. This run starts from the best checkpoint observed in the first L4 run rather than the later terminal checkpoint, lowers PPO learning rate to 1e-4, adds a tiny write penalty to reduce shared-byte spam, and uses 16-episode best-eval selection to reduce checkpoint-selection noise. Ant slot/rank 0 starts active at step 0, then one additional rank is released every 150 environment steps. The existing 8-way actor identity tail is interpreted as release rank, so the checkpoint loads without actor-shape changes. Inactive ants are hidden from ant-count observations, forced to stay/write zero, excluded from PPO actor loss, and omitted from rendering until released. Runtime profile uses the L4-selected 128x256 rollout shape. Training keeps the source 0.75 movement temperature; held-out eval and rendering use 0.52 for sharper movement inspection."
